From 4be445e6898f481ed8dfe9aa4ac3a3a45efa0b0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:20:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] sycl: XMX flash attention: q8_0 K/V, and row groups for
 longer drafts

q8_0 K/V: a second kernel dequantizes straight into the XMX operand registers. An operand
register holds one tile column per lane (lane l: column l, element i: row i), so the products
are arranged for each lane to read consecutive bytes of one KV cell: S = Q K^T with K^T as the
B operand (16 consecutive dims of the lane's cell) and O^T += V^T P^T with V^T as the A operand
(8 consecutive dims); P is kept transposed in SLM. Its many small loads want more work-groups
in flight than f16 (8 per Xe core against 2). The q8_0 decode path was the vector kernel,
reading the K/V once per query head.

Row groups: a verify step with more drafted tokens has more Q rows than one 16-row tile
(GQA 6 x 3 tokens = 18); those now take up to 4 row groups of whole tokens, which run side by
side over the same KV range (so all but the first read it from L2), instead of the tile kernel.

Each variant is its own SYCL kernel: one kernel holding both was register-allocated for the
q8_0 path and cost the f16 one 3-20 %.

tests: q8_0 flash attention for 1-3 tokens at GQA 4/6/8 and head size 128/256, several
sequences, heads interleaved in a row, another sequence's cells masked; perf at 3 and 4
tokens (f16) and 1/2 tokens and a 512-token prefill with q8_0 K/V.

Arc Pro B70, head dim 256, 4 K/V heads, GQA 6 (us), f16 tile -> XMX: 64k KV, 3 tokens
1729 -> 511, 4 tokens 1733 -> 528; 16k 506 / 516 -> 151 / 157; 1-2 tokens as before (475 / 490
at 64k). q8_0 vector/tile -> XMX: 64k KV 1 token 5474 -> 548, 2 tokens 7001 -> 560; 16k 1178 /
1563 -> 151 / 159. FLASH_ATTN_EXT 4125/4125 (145 cases on the XMX kernels).
